---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const lang = 'en' as const;
---
<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="Install REA (rea-agents) — community guide | rea.run"
  description="Install REA with npx rea-agents setup, MCP registration, and bring-your-own Ghidra. Paraphrase of upstream docs; verify on GitHub."
  path="/docs/install/"
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <p class="badge">Docs · Install</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)]">Install REA</h1>
    <p class="mt-4">
      Community paraphrase of upstream get-started / installation notes. Product behavior is defined by
      <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea">morluto/rea</a> and
      <a href="https://morluto.github.io/rea/get-started/">official get-started</a>. Versions change — re-check before you automate.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Authorized use only.</strong> Install and run REA against software you have the right to analyze. No crack or DRM bypass guidance here.
    </div>

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Node.js <strong>22</strong> (22.19+), <strong>24</strong> (24.11+), or <strong>26+</strong>, plus npm (per upstream).</li>
      <li>An MCP-capable coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Windsurf, Grok Build, and others listed upstream), or the CLI alone.</li>
      <li>For deep <strong>native</strong> analysis: an existing Hopper, Ghidra, or IDA setup as documented upstream. Static JavaScript / Electron inspection does not need those engines.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Connect your coding agent</h2>
    <p>Ask your agent to run setup with approval, or run it yourself:</p>
    <pre><code>npx rea-agents@latest setup</code></pre>
    <p>
      Choose your client, review the plan, and approve changes. Setup registers the MCP server and matching investigation skill, backing up existing config. <strong>Restart the client</strong> afterward.
    </p>
    <p>Manual MCP registration shape (confirm against upstream if your client needs hand-edited JSON):</p>
    <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "rea": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "rea-agents@latest", "mcp"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
    <p>Pin an exact <code>rea-agents@VERSION</code> when you need reproducible installs.</p>

    <h2>Optional: global CLI</h2>
    <pre><code>npm install --global rea-agents</code></pre>

    <h2>Ghidra (bring your own)</h2>
    <p>REA does not install Ghidra or Java. Export absolute paths, then doctor + setup:</p>
    <pre><code>{`export GHIDRA_INSTALL_DIR=/absolute/path/to/ghidra_PUBLIC
export JAVA_HOME=/absolute/path/to/jdk-21
npx -y rea-agents@latest doctor --provider ghidra --json
npx rea-agents@latest setup`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Upstream documents supported host/Ghidra/JDK combinations. Prefer the exact versions listed in
      <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/installation.md">docs/installation.md</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>First question to try</h2>
    <p>After reconnecting the agent, give an <strong>absolute path</strong> to a target you may analyze and a specific question (entry points, export paths, a named feature). Prefer Evidence + unknowns over speculative narratives.</p>

    <h2>Upstream links</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://morluto.github.io/rea/get-started/">Official get-started</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/rea-agents">npm: rea-agents</a></li>
      <li><a href="/blog/ghidra-mcp-with-rea/">Community: Ghidra MCP with REA</a></li>
      <li><a href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
